# UI Primitive Consolidation Plan

## Context
Targeted migrations created useful Button, Select, Checkbox, Input, and Tile
components, but the 2026-08-27 whole-frontend audit found that the foundation is
still split between `components/input` and `components/ui`, has no focused tests
for its core controls, and coexists with global `.btn`, local card/action systems,
402 raw buttons, and 64 `unstyled` escapes. This plan is now sequence index 1 for
`frontend_maintainability_normalization_sequence` and owns the canonical
foundation before broad decomposition or migration begins.

## Goal
- Consolidate scattered UI elements into reusable, consistent primitive components.
- Maximize UI consistency across all routes.
- Replace naked HTML tags with typed, beautifully styled React primitives.
- Establish `components/ui/` as the single foundation owner, with deliberate
  form adapters in `components/form/` and temporary compatibility re-exports.
- Cover foundation semantics, keyboard/focus behavior, disabled/loading states,
  controlled/uncontrolled behavior, and accessibility with focused tests.

## Non-Goals
- Complete redesign of the entire app visual language.
- Rewriting backend APIs or non-UI business logic.

## Steps
1. Create/refactor foundation primitives in `src/components/ui/` or `src/components/input/`.
   - `Button`: variants (primary, secondary, danger, ghost, outline), sizes (sm, md, lg, icon).
   - `Select`: variants (standard, minimal), fix custom arrow placement, improve dropdown spacing.
   - `Checkbox`: custom SVG checkmark, unified border-radius, consistent label spacing.
   - `Tile` / `Card`: variants (interactive, static), defined border radius, background colors, and effects.
2. Refactor Core Routes (Admin, Settings, Auth).
   - Replace `<select>`, `<button>`, and `<input type="checkbox">` instances in `Admin Dashboard`, `MetaControlPanel`, `ProfileSettings`, `SecuritySettings`, and `Auth` screens.
3. Builder & Editor Standardization.
   - Convert the `Component Picker` UI in Datasource Editor to use the new `<Select>` and `<Tile>` primitives.
   - Refactor Page Builder block configuration forms (`CardDesigner`, `ColumnMapper`, `DerivedSectionBlock`).
4. Foundation CSS token standardization.
   - Ensure primitive styles use the shared color, border, background, focus,
     radius, typography, and spacing tokens.
   - Remove legacy inline styles and one-off classes from migrated call sites.
   - Hand repository-wide token drift, global `.btn` removal, and unrelated
     inline-style ownership to sequence index 2 rather than duplicating its scope.
5. Canonical foundation realignment.
   - Move Button, Select, Checkbox, and Tile authority into `components/ui/`.
   - Rename the current generic `Input` to its real composer responsibility and
     add deliberate text-field/textarea primitives rather than overloading it.
   - Reconcile global `.btn` and overlapping Tile/Card/ContentFlatCard/GlassCard
     contracts into one semantic action and surface vocabulary.
   - Add shared dialog/menu/tabs/feedback primitives only where the inventory
     proves repeated interaction ownership; retain specialized domain behavior.
   - Add focused tests and a compatibility path for later sequence members.

## Verification
- Confirm 0 raw `<button>`, `<select>`, and `<input type="checkbox">` elements remain in core routes (grep search).
- Verify all interactive states (hover, focus, disabled) map accurately across new components.
- Verify typescript checks pass completely after refactor.

